The body-sensitivity result is decisive: after changing only the base return to `"X"`, trusted CPython and fixed K execution return `"X"` for `"bab"`, yet the extended proof still proves the concrete false result `"a"` and the universal long-string claim as `#Top`. This witnesses that the nested-call rule imports the desired answer instead of deriving it.

I’m also extending the fidelity corpus across CPython’s recursion boundary, because the source contract has no length restriction and the submitted implementation is recursive.
